 "area": "retina",
 "description": "BLOCK 215000 -- SPITE-TO-SUCCEED: a GRIEVANCE (an appraised slight from a specific rival) AMPLIFIES the value of the agent's OWN achievement -- the CONSTRUCTIVE face of spite (underdog / chip-on-shoulder / vindication), nearly the inverse of destructive spite (harm-the-other-at-self-cost, block 213000). Every decision is a RULE over the LANDED 204000 core_emotions economy: gs_choose_action is Argmax_c (total_value(c) + amp(c)) over the agent's candidate Appraisals; the amplification amp is the ONLY new term and it is graph data. The grievance magnitude is a LEAKY ACCUMULATOR -- a Sum of 196000 scale2 (Ashr, x2^-k) decayed slight contributions, idempotent under the run_rules fixpoint (a pure function of immutable Slight nodes + adapter-advanced now_epoch). Efficacy gates the CHANNEL: HIGH efficacy (>=5, a viable path to win) fires gs_amplify_succeed -> amp = G*max(0,effort-rival_ach)*observed_by_rival, raising OWN competence candidates (self-benefiting, directed, witnessed); LOW efficacy fires gs_amplify_destroy -> amp = G*rival_harm on the destroy candidates (self-costly, ties 213000). The SAME grievance, one knob (efficacy), flips succeed<->destroy. Integer-native (Sum/Ashr/IDiv/Max/Times/Plus/Minus/Gte/Eq/And/Not/Argmax/Attr; no Rust, no new Term). OFF by default: self_load_only, nothing depends_on it, every rule guards on HeldGrievanceParams.enabled -- absent it every existing path is byte-identical. A glass-box named-knob MODEL of the underdog effect; the contribution is the attribution + the efficacy-gates-channel unification of constructive vs destructive spite, not new psychology.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "grievance_succeed",
  "description": "A grievance is a leaky accumulator built from appraised slights by a specific rival; it re-weights the agent's OWN achievement valuation. Efficacy (competence-belief) is the switch: with a path to win the grievance drives constructive success (vindication); with no path the same grievance collapses into destructive spite."
 },
